# The inverse image of an ideal sheaf on a small affine open of the source

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a morphism of schemes, `I` an ideal sheaf on `X`, `U` an affine open of `X`
and `V` an affine open of `Y` contained in `f⁻¹(U)`. Then the ideal that `I.comap f` cuts out on
`V` is generated by the image of `I.ideal U` under the restriction map `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(Y, V)`. That
is `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_appLE`, stated in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DivisorFlatPullback.Basic` and re-exported here, where the Tag
0806 lifting argument uses it.

Mathlib computes the components of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.comap` only for an
open immersion (`ideal_comap_of_isOpenImmersion`), and
`Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_of_isAffineHom` computes them for an affine morphism, but only on
the *whole* preimage `f⁻¹(U)`, which is affine exactly because `f` is assumed affine. The form
re-exported here needs no hypothesis on `f` at all: once `V` is an affine open of `Y` inside
`f⁻¹(U)`, the restriction `f.resLE U V` is a morphism of affine schemes, which is the only
situation `Stacks.IdealSheaf.ideal_comap_top_of_isAffine` needs.

